<header><p class="st-kicker">prince bishopric · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Bishopric of Culm</h1><p class="st-meta">1243 CE – 1466 CE · capital Löbau</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the four Prussian dioceses set up in 1243, ruling the land of Löbau and passing under the Polish crown in 1466.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1243 the papal legate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-of-modena">William of Modena</a> divided conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> into four dioceses: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chelmno">Culm</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pomesanians">Pomesania</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-warmia">Warmia</a> and Samland. Culm covered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chelmno-land">Chełmno land</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konrad-i-of-masovia">Konrad of Masovia</a> had granted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> received a third of the diocese as his own territory, chiefly around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubawa">Löbau</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a>' cathedral stood at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chelmza">Culmsee</a> (Chełmża), while they resided at the castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubawa">Löbau</a>. The cathedral chapter was incorporated into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> in the 13th century, tying the bishopric closely to the Order's state. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chelmno-law">Chełmno law</a>, granted in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chelmno">Culm</a> charter of 1233, became the model for town and land rights across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>During the Thirteen Years' War, the Prussian estates rebelled against the Order, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-peace-of-thorn">Second Peace of Thorn</a> in 1466 placed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chelmno-land">Chełmno land</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Polish crown</a> as part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/royal-prussia">Royal Prussia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> became Polish senators, and the diocese continued as a church province.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bishopric-of-culm.jpg" alt="Bishopric of Culm" width="320" height="427"><figcaption>Image: Mateuszgdynia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bazylika_konkatedralna_%C5%9Bw._Tr%C3%B3jcy_w_Che%C5%82m%C5%BCy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1243 CE – 1466 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>prince bishopric</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Löbau</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Heidenreich</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Low German, Latin, Polish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bishopric of Chełmno, Bistum Kulm</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1354&amp;focus=bishopric-of-culm" aria-label="Bishopric of Culm on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5095 347 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bishopric of Culm lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5415 603L5451 561M5415 603L5457 692"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5451 561h0M5457 692h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5415 603h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5415 603h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1354&amp;focus=bishopric-of-culm">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
